vkd3d: invalidate root descriptors when changing root signature

Steel Nomad Light sends an old raw VA (VK_DESCRIPTOR_TYPE_MAX_ENUM) as a
push descriptor after switching root signatures. Clearing the active mask
prevents emission of stale arguments. Redundant same-signature binds retain
state, as required by D3D12; later explicit root binds become active normally.

--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -14648,6 +14648,10 @@
     if (bindings->root_signature == root_signature)
         return;
 
+    /* A different root signature invalidates all previous root arguments.
+     * In particular, an active raw-VA SRV from the old signature must not
+     * become a uniform-buffer push descriptor in the new signature. */
+    bindings->root_descriptor_active_mask = 0;
     bindings->root_signature = root_signature;
     bindings->static_sampler_set = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
 
